  "description": "todo-touch.md 7.1, on the bench Harmony Touch holding work/touch-firmware/sets/6.9-label-back (the recorded full sync's documents under tags of ours, 6.8 and 6.9). Every expectation is derived from those documents by packages/bench/src/touchengine.ts, a model of the engine read in the firmware, and named as the monitor names a code of the Touch's own documents. Step 1 presses Off so no activity runs and the engine holds every device off; what it sends depends on what ran before and is not judged. Each device is chosen from the Devices list with no activity running, and every key its own map binds is tapped, then every key with a long press held about 1 s. Predicted per key: the command the device's own map binds, to that device; activities play no part. Devices whose map binds no key are left out: Switch. A tap held too long sends the long command instead: repeat the step and note it.",
